      <statement><p>Use the following figure, which shows a graph of <m>f(x)</m> to find each of
the indicated integrals.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/webwork-19-image-1.png" width="33%"/>
<p><em>(Click on the graph for a larger version.)</em></p>
<p>Note that the first area (with vertical, red shading) is 24 and the
second (with oblique, black shading) is 8.</p>
<p><alert>A.</alert>
<m>\int_a^b f(x) dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert>B.</alert>
<m>\int_b^c f(x) dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert>C.</alert>
<m>\int_a^c f(x) dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><alert>D.</alert>
<m>\int_a^c |f(x)| dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>24</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>-8</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>16</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>32</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><m>y = f(x)</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis, with area below the axis being
counted as negative area.  Therefore



<m>\int_a^b f(x) dx = 24</m>,
<m>\int_b^c f(x) dx = -8</m>,
<m>\int_a^c f(x) dx = 24  - 8 = 16</m>, and
<m>\int_a^c |f(x)| dx = |24| + |-8| = 32</m>.



</solution>
