      <statement><p>Find the average value of 
<m>f(x)=4 x + 8</m> over <m>[3,6]</m></p>
<p>average value = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>26</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><m>f</m> on
<m>3\le x\le 6</m>.  The integral is the area under the curve, which is a 
trapezoidal area.  So the average value is
<me>\mbox{average} = \frac1{6-3} \int_{3}^{6} (4 x+8)\,dx = 
  \frac1{3}\cdot\frac{20+32}{2}\cdot 3 = 26.</me>



</solution>
