      <statement><p>The following table gives the the approximate amount of emissions, 
<m>E</m>, of nitrogen oxides in millions of metric tons per year in the US.
Let <m>t</m> be the number of years since 1940 and <m>E=f(t)</m>.</p>
<tabular bottom="minor" left="minor" top="major" valign="top">
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<row bottom="minor">
<cell/>
<cell>1940</cell>
<cell>1950</cell>
<cell>1960</cell>
<cell>1970</cell>
<cell>1980</cell>
<cell>1990</cell>
</row>
<row bottom="minor">
<cell><m>t</m></cell>
<cell>0</cell>
<cell>10</cell>
<cell>20</cell>
<cell>30</cell>
<cell>40</cell>
<cell>50</cell>
</row>
<row bottom="major">
<cell><m>E</m></cell>
<cell>7</cell>
<cell>9</cell>
<cell>12.8</cell>
<cell>18.8</cell>
<cell>21</cell>
<cell>19.4</cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p>Estimate the integral: <m>\int_0^{50}{f(t)dt} \approx</m> 
<fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><em>Be sure that you know what the units of your answer are, and
what its meaning is!</em></p>
<p><em>(Original data from the Statistical Abstract of the US,
1992)</em></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>No correct answer specified</p>
      </answer>
      <solution><p>The integral <m>\int_0^{50}{f(t)dt}</m> represents the total
emissions of nitrogen oxides, in millions of metric tons, during
the period 1940 to 1990.</p>
<p>We estimate the integral using left- and right-hand sums:
<me>\mbox{Left sum} = (7)(10) + (9)(10) + 
  (12.8)(10) + (18.8)(10) + (21)(10) = 
  686,</me>
and
<me>\mbox{Right sum} = (9)(10) + (12.8)(10) + 
  (18.8)(10) + (21)(10) + (19.4)(10) = 
  810.</me>
We can then average the
left- and right-hand sums to find the best estimate of the
integral:
<me>\int_0^{50}{f(t)dt} \approx {{686 + 810} \over 2} = 748
\mbox{ million metric tons.}</me>
Between 1940 and 1990,
about 748 million metric tons of nitrogen oxides were emitted.</p>
</solution>
