      <statement><p>Calculate the integral approximations <m>T_{6}</m> , <m>M_{6}</m> and <m>S_{12}</m> for</p>
<p><m>\int^{7}_{2} x^{4} \, dx</m>.</p>
<p><m>T_{6}</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>M_{6}</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>S_{12}</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>3432.46</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>3316.3</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>3355.02</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><m>f(x) = x^{4}</m>.  We divide [2, 7] into 6 subintervals of width



<m>\Delta x = \frac{7 - 2}{6} = 0.833333</m>



with endpoints <m>x_i</m> = 2, 2.83333, 3.66667, 4.5, 5.33333, 6.16667, 7, and midpoints <m>c_j</m> = 2.41667, 3.25, 4.08333, 4.91667, 5.75, 6.58333.  With this data, we get



<m>T_{6} = \frac{1}{2} \Delta x \left( f(x_0) + 2  f(x_1) + ... + 2  f(x_{N-1}) + f(x_N) \right) = \frac{1}{2} \cdotp 0.833333 \left( 16 + 128.89 + 361.506 + 820.125 + 1618.17 + 2892.22 + 2401 \right) = 3432.46</m>



<m>M_{6} = \Delta x \left( f(c_1) + ... + f(c_N) \right) =  0.833333 \left( 34.1088 + 111.566 + 278.009 + 584.363 + 1093.13 + 1878.38 \right) = 3316.3</m>



<m>S_{12} = \frac{2 M_{6}+T_{6}}{3}  = 3355.02</m>


</solution>
